CORE
test.c
--nondet-volatile
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
OUTPUT address_of\("volatile-write"
--
--
Phase 1 of the MMIO device-environment model. A volatile read is
non-deterministic (the device may change the register), so the read-back
assertion fails; and a volatile write is preserved as an observable side
effect, emitted as an OUTPUT instruction so it is not sliced away.
